# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# The router binary, when built in place. The private repo this was extracted
# from had a 20MB compiled binary checked in.
/discrimen

# Calibration output from `discrimen bench calibrate`. It is a per-fleet
# measurement, not a source artefact — pool.json and benchmark_data.go are the
# committed halves of that pipeline.
# calibration.json* — the trailing glob catches the .bak a purge leaves behind,
# which is the same per-fleet measurement and slipped into a commit once.
internal/router/benchdata/calibration.json*

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Python bytecode from the embeddings worker
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Private coding test blobs: ~250MB of base64(zlib(pickle)) fetched beside
# pool.json. Reproducible from `discrimen bench fetch`, so not a source artefact.
internal/router/benchdata/private/
